# Code Style Standards

## Comments Policy

- Write self-documenting code with clear variable and function names
- **ALWAYS preserve function/method docstrings** - these are essential for API documentation
- Only add inline comments for:
  - Complex algorithms or business logic
  - Non-obvious "why" decisions (never "what" the code does)
  - Important edge cases or gotchas
- NO trivial inline comments that restate code
- NO comments for simple operations, imports, or obvious logic
- **Function docstrings should include**: Args, Returns, and brief description when not obvious

## General Principles

- Follow DRY, KISS, and YAGNI
- Prefer functional patterns over OOP where appropriate
- Keep functions small and focused (max 50 lines)
- Use explicit error handling - never silent failures
- Type everything (TypeScript strict mode, Python type hints)

## Spacing & Formatting

- NO excessive blank lines - maximum 1 blank line between code blocks
- NO blank lines at start/end of functions
- Use blank lines only to separate logical sections
